### Final Code & Model Review

I have reviewed the final code in [`dispatch_gate.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/dispatch_gate.rs) and [`dispatcher.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs) against the checklist and supplied verification evidence (which is treated strictly as external server-provided evidence, as no commands or tests were executed during this read-only review).

#### 1. Queue `Gate` Races & Coalesced Release/Acquire Publication ([`dispatch_gate.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/dispatch_gate.rs#L12-L66))
- **`pending()` Fix:** [`Gate::pending`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/dispatch_gate.rs#L49-L62) now cleanly transitions `RUNNING | NOTIFIED -> QUEUED` and `RUNNING -> IDLE` using an `AcqRel` CAS loop and returns `next == QUEUED`. It is invoked in [`Job::poll`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L120-L126) strictly *after* dropping the `future` `MutexGuard`, ensuring any concurrent wake either sets `NOTIFIED` prior to `pending()` (causing the polling worker to re-enqueue) or observes `IDLE` after `pending()` and enqueues the job itself.
- **Coalesced Wake Publication:** [`Gate::notify`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/dispatch_gate.rs#L18-L40) preserves the unconditional `Ordering::AcqRel` `compare_exchange_weak` even when transitioning `QUEUED -> QUEUED` or `RUNNING | NOTIFIED -> RUNNING | NOTIFIED`, returning `enqueue = (state == IDLE)`. Because RMW operations participate in the release sequence on the atomic state variable, any data written before a coalesced `notify()` is properly published (`Release`) and observed (`Acquire`) by the next worker calling [`Gate::claim`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/dispatch_gate.rs#L42-L46) (either directly on `QUEUED -> RUNNING`, or transitively across `notify (AcqRel) -> pending (AcqRel) -> claim (AcqRel)`).
- **Completion Terminal State:** [`Gate::complete`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/dispatch_gate.rs#L63-L65) stores `DONE` (`Release`) after `future.take()` and unlocking, permanently blocking any subsequent `notify()` or `claim()`.
- **Loom Coverage:** All four Loom models in [`loom_tests`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/dispatch_gate.rs#L68-L167)—[`wake_during_or_after_pending_is_enqueued_once`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/dispatch_gate.rs#L73-L94), [`duplicate_wakes_do_not_duplicate_entries`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/dispatch_gate.rs#L96-L115), [`coalesced_wake_publishes_data_to_the_next_poll`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/dispatch_gate.rs#L117-L152) (for both `already_running` states), and [`wake_while_completing_never_resurrects_future`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/dispatch_gate.rs#L154-L166)—accurately model the state transitions and memory ordering requirements.

#### 2. Destructor Safety, Thread Shutdown, Self-Join, and `ids` Callback Growth ([`dispatcher.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs))
- **`ids` Tracking & Retired Blocking Helpers:** [`Pool::new`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L170-L176) registers both `.on_thread_start` and `.on_thread_stop` callbacks on the Tokio runtime builder so retired blocking helper threads remove their `ThreadId`s instead of growing `ids` unboundedly (covered by [`retired_blocking_helpers_do_not_accumulate_thread_ids`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L750-L789)).
- **Self-Shutdown Prevention:** [`Pool::shutdown`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L500-L505) checks `self.ids` up front and rejects calls coming from any native worker, reactor owner, or Tokio runtime/blocking thread, preventing self-join deadlocks.
- **Bounded Teardown & Thread Cleanup:** [`Pool::shutdown`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L506-L522) waits up to `SHUTDOWN_LIMIT` (5s) for active [`Lease`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L65-L72) counts to reach zero before setting `state.closed = true`. [`Pool::close_workers`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L473-L499) then sets `closed`, notifies/unparks all workers, joins every native worker and removes its `ThreadId`, drops `tokio_jobs` and signals `reactor_stop`, joins the `owner` thread (which invokes `runtime.shutdown_timeout(SHUTDOWN_LIMIT)`), removes the owner `ThreadId`, and verifies `panicked == false && remaining == 0`—returning an `io::Error` if any worker panicked or any blocking helper threads remain alive.
- **Unwind & Destructor Ordering:** In [`Job::poll`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L103-L137), `Reset` is a guard that restores the `POLLING` thread-local even on panic; the future is taken and its mutex unlocked *before* `self.gate.complete()` and before `drop(finished)` is executed inside `catch_unwind`. Dropping the completed future outside the lock avoids lock-order inversions and safely releases its `Lease` (which decrements `active.count` and notifies `idle`).

#### 3. Startup Settings Cache, Queue Policies, and Deadlock Freedom ([`dispatcher.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs))
- **Startup Settings Cache:** [`spawn`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L545-L587) parses `SPAWNED_EXPERIMENT_WORKERS`, `SPAWNED_EXPERIMENT_REACTORS`, and `SPAWNED_EXPERIMENT_LOCAL_BUDGET` once when initializing the singleton `Pool` inside `registry()`, validating ranges and returning `io::ErrorKind::InvalidInput` errors instead of panicking or reading environment variables on actor hot paths.
- **Global / Local / Steal / TokioPool Policies & Lock Ordering:**
  - `Policy::Global` waits on `self.ready.wait(queues)` in [`Pool::run`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-fede-controls/rt/src/tasks/experimental/dispatcher.rs#L388-L430) without scanning local queues or polling on a 1ms timeout.
  - Lock acquisition is never nested across `registry()`, `active`, `queues`, `split[i]`, `workers`, `ids`, `reactor_stop`, `owner`, `tokio_jobs`, or `Job::future`.

---

### Verdict

**APPROVE** — No blocking issues remain. The `dispatch_gate` and experimental `dispatcher` implementations are approved for experimental measurement.
